    "offset_source": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11214-020-00758-8",
    "offset_status": "Illustrative radiative/advection scaling inspired by the published trend. The 1500 K normalization is a scenario choice. Values are not extracted Showman et al. GCM predictions.",
    "map": "Degree-2 map made from (1 - fraction) times a uniform map plus fraction times a projected spherical Gaussian. The default width is 40 degrees and the injected fraction is 0.8. Recovery fits separate uniform and hotspot amplitudes. A dense-sphere positivity bound limits their ratio. Map normalization uses the target's subobserver latitude.",
    "noise": "Independent white Gaussian noise. Explicit noise_levels_ppm values are per noise_reference_seconds (default 60 seconds) and are scaled by the square root of reference time over exposure time. No ETC or red-noise model.",
    "visit": "Symmetric continuous visit centered on the supplied eclipse time, with cadence and exposure from each target. Full-window and occulted-exposure-only fits are saved separately. The forward orbit uses transit t0 half a period before the eclipse center, and the subobserver latitude follows inclination.",
    "limitations": [
      "Fixed circular orbit and supplied geometry; no orbit uncertainty.",
      "The injection and recovery use the same degree-2 Gaussian template family.",
      "Profile-grid screening with BIC weights; this is not full posterior inference.",
      "The uniform-null control has no injected hotspot and tests false map detections.",
      "Only selected scenarios are simulated; omitted scenarios are not run controls."
    ]
  },
  "input_assumptions": {
    "noise": "User-authorized white noise scenarios at 50 and 100 ppm per ideal 60 second bin; not ETC prediction",
